            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0317" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/480</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State (Castle)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-01">September 1, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Italian Ambassador read me a short telegram from the Italian Ambassador in
                    Tokyo reporting on a conversation he had had with the Russian Ambassador in that
                    capital; the Russian Ambassador told him that the Russian Government would find
                    no difficulty in recognizing the independence of Manchukuo; he added to this
                    that he hoped that, after both Japan and Russia had recognized Manchukuo, Japan
                    would be willing to sign a non-aggression treaty with Russia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >W. R. Castle, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
